	(text "ARACHNE-18 MINI BRAIN v1.0 - ESP32-S3 + MPU-6050 hexapod servo controller for a Raspberry Pi 4 (generated by tools/build_sch.py from tools/design.py)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 552 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e8f54849-ecb3-522e-b859-d1dcb5f6995f")
	)
	(text "Servo connectors: 1 = GND, 2 = +12 V, 3 = DATA (Feetech STS half-duplex bus, 1 Mbaud). CHECK the pin order against your cable before plugging in!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 556 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f62db6b6-db4d-5c92-bf3f-7ec0f33ff615")
	)
	(text "Bus A = legs L1 L2 L3 (ESP32 UART1: TX IO17, RX IO18, DE IO16).  Bus B = legs L4 L5 L6 (UART2: TX IO10, RX IO11, DE IO9). DE = RTS in RS485 half-duplex mode."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 560 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "66b544e9-e558-59c3-ba3f-e8a0f0920500")
	)
	(text "Pi 4 link: USB-C (board) <-> USB-A (Pi) cable on the ESP32-S3 native USB -> /dev/ttyACM0 on the Pi. Pi VBUS only feeds the ESP32 (through D7), never the servos."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 564 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e63eeb66-4ee8-5762-87f2-e9e7b2c23254")
	)
	(text "5V PI pads: buck output (5 V, 3 A for the Pi 4) -> Pi GPIO pin 2/4 (+5V) and 6 (GND), or a cut USB-C lead into the Pi power socket."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 568 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "17d5fa99-75e4-5b14-9916-d99b21204ae0")
	)
	(text "Buck = TI TPS54560B datasheet design (fig. 32): 400 kHz, 5.0 V 5 A. UVLO start 6.5 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 572 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0380199d-682c-5cd8-91c7-3a3a433c6901")
	)
